    "details": "<p><code class=\"language-html\"><code class=\"language-html\"></code></code></p>\n<p><strong>ESCAPE THE SERVER &mdash; <em>The Farewell</em></strong></p>\n<p>At 03:41 AM, SERVER EPOCH-01 began erasing itself. By morning, Dr. Meera Kapoor was gone and so was the truth. You have sixty minutes at her terminal. Recover the server. Then work out who was standing behind her.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">They threw her a farewell party. Cake, speeches, a card everyone signed. She stayed late, the way she always did.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Nobody knows exactly when the building emptied. What is known is that sometime after midnight, someone walked through corridors that should have been locked, sat down at a machine that wasn't theirs, and started giving a database orders it was never supposed to take. By 03:41 AM, SERVER EPOCH-01 was eating itself alive. Meera Kapoor never made it out of the building.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">The logs survived. Some of them. So did her workstation, still sitting in recovery mode behind a password only she would have chosen.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">You are the recovery squad. Sixty minutes on the clock, a wipe bar climbing toward irreversible, and a machine full of half-erased evidence.Every single clue you recover will point somewhere, and most of them are pointing exactly where someone wanted them to point.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Stop the wipe and you save the data. Read it properly and you save an innocent person from taking the fall.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Both, or neither. The console locks at 2:25 PM.</p>\n<p><strong>Eligibility</strong>:</p>\n<p>Open to all college students.</p>\n<p><strong>Format:</strong></p>\n<p>The event follows a five-lock technical escape-room format. Each team works through the locks in the designated sequence. The core mission window is <strong style=\"color: #000000;\">60 minutes</strong>. Teams may use hints carrying a point penalty.</p>\n<p><strong>Duration:</strong></p>\n<p>The event is scheduled from <strong>12:30 PM to 2:00 PM on 12th September 2026</strong>. The participant session includes check-in, story briefing, station setup, a 60-minute mission, and final submission.</p>\n<p><strong>Team Size:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>2&ndash;5 members per team.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each team must consist of 2&ndash;5 members.</li>\n<li>Teams must complete the five technical locks in the designated sequence.</li>\n<li>Participants must solve the challenges using their own technical and logical reasoning skills.</li>\n<li>Teams must complete the mission within the allotted time.</li>\n<li>Participants must follow all instructions provided by the event organizers and row volunteers.</li>\n<li>Any attempt to interfere with another team&rsquo;s progress, console, or event infrastructure will result in immediate disqualification.</li>\n<li>Teams must use only the resources, hints, and systems permitted by the organizers.</li>\n<li>Outside devices or pre-shared answers are not permitted.</li>\n<li>Each team is allotted 3 hints for the full mission; each hint carries a point penalty.</li>\n<li>The decision of the organizing team regarding event results is final and binding.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Venue:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Computer Lab F-203, NMIMS Chandigarh.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Capacity:</strong></p>\n<p>60 participants</p>\n<p><strong>Total Prize Pool:</strong> ₹6,000, plus certificates for winners and participation certificates for all participants.</p>\n<p><code class=\"language-html\">\n</code></p>",
